1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:14,832
Welcome to Nomikos Synergathis. This is a new recording of the
real local application, using a synthetic tax policy and a
dedicated demo account. Two questions will be sent to the
configured AI provider.

2
00:00:14,832 --> 00:00:30,409
We open a previously analyzed three-page document. The overview
presents the findings, document profile, evidence quality, and a
human-review warning. This is a real saved case, not a populated
visual mockup.

3
00:00:30,409 --> 00:00:45,305
The facts and obligations section is empty in this particular
saved analysis. The original document does contain requirements,
so these zero counts expose an extraction issue rather than
proving that no obligations exist.

4
00:00:45,305 --> 00:00:58,077
The timeline also shows the available extracted dates. In this
case the saved analysis has not extracted calendar dates, another
limitation to review against the original document.

5
00:00:58,077 --> 00:01:13,059
Risk radar contains five findings with suggested mitigations and
links to cited excerpts. These are model-assisted findings and
require human checking, especially because optical character
recognition may introduce errors.

6
00:01:13,059 --> 00:01:26,066
The action plan and decision center are also part of the
workspace. This saved case has zero extracted actions and
decisions; the demo shows those empty states rather than
inventing results.

7
00:01:26,066 --> 00:01:38,463
The evidence view links claims to source fragments and flags
material that needs review. A citation or an automated label is
not proof: the reader must inspect the original page.

8
00:01:38,463 --> 00:01:58,589
First we ask the document assistant for deadlines and owners.
This is a real streamed AI answer with page citations. The
automatic evidence check was unavailable. The OCR also reports
July sixteen where the original document says July fifteen,
showing why source review matters.

9
00:01:58,589 --> 00:02:17,615
Next we ask about risks and proposed actions. The retrieved
excerpt did not contain the relevant details, so the answer
missed information present elsewhere in the document. This
reveals a retrieval limitation. Both questions used synthetic
data and real provider calls.
